ry_7", "content": " Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking to Repeat"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Use these expressions to ask a person to repeat what they said.  You ask a person to repeat, to clarify or confirm what you hear. <br> <br> <span class=\"strong\">Asking a person to repeat:</span><br> Could you repeat that, please?<br>What was that?<br>Sorry? I didn't catch that.</span> <br><br>Use yes/no questions to ask a person to repeat, clarify and confirm.<br><br><span class = \"strong\">Michael</span>: I am lost!<br/><span class = \"strong\">Clerk</span>: What was that?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Michael</span>: I'm lost! <br/><br/>Remember: If you ask a yes/no question, use rising intonation.\u000b"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">Sara</span>: My name is Sara.<br/><span class = \"strong\">Boss</span>: Is your name Zara?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Sara</span>: No, it's Sara"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making and Responding to Requests"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use phrases that include modals to make and respond to requests:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Making a Request\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could you\u2026?</span> <br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can you\u2026?</span> <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Would you mind\u2026?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Responding to a Request\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Sure. No problem.</span> <br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'd love to.</span> <br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Yes, no problem.</span> <br><Br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Sorry, I can't.</span> <br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm sorry, I can't.</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Customs Officer</span>: Can you give me your customs declaration form, please? <span class=\"strong\"><br>Vanessa</span>: Sure."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">Sally</span>: Would you mind if I sat beside you?<br><span class = \"strong\">John</span>: No, please join me!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to stay"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "where you will be living"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Where are you staying?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Use these words to talk about customs at the airport."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "restricted"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "banned; you can't have it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you have any restricted items?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to declare"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to officially say the value of items you have"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you have anything to declare?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "duty free shop"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a store that sells goods tax-free to travellers who are leaving the country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I always shop at the Duty Free shop."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inspection"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of checking carefully"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Please bring your bag for inspection."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to inspect"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to check carefully, usually by an official"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have to inspect your bags."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le09ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read each role card."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose one role."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice the situation with your partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch roles and practice again."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Role 1:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You are a customs officer. Ask the traveler 3 questions. For example: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Where are you staying? Where are you coming from? Do you have anything to declare?</span> You have to inspect their bag.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Role 2:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are a traveler. You answer the customs officer's questions.